<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Earhart returns ten weeks after her first visit. She has used the saline rinses twice daily and fluticasone every morning throughout, and finished the amoxicillin-clavulanate course seven weeks ago. The discolored drainage has not come back, but her nose is still blocked most days, the left cheek pressure returns when she bends forward, and her sense of smell is still poor. The left ear that was injured on the flight four weeks ago cleared after about ten days and her hearing is back to normal. Her dentist found no dental problem last week. Her HIV and hepatitis C tests from the preventive visit were negative. She has not flown since the barotrauma. Her sinus CT was done this morning, and Dr. Lindgren reviewed it with her in the otolaryngology clinic before this visit. SNOT-22 today 41. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medical therapy</td><td>Ten weeks of saline irrigation and fluticasone; antibiotic course finished seven weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Blockage most days, left cheek pressure, poor smell; no discolored drainage</td></tr><tr><td>Scores</td><td>SNOT-22 41; facial pain 4 of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Ear</td><td>Cleared after about ten days; hearing normal</td></tr><tr><td>Other results</td><td>Dental check normal; HIV and hepatitis C negative</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

